      {
        "id": 81564,
        "name": "Benhimself",
        "username": "Benhimself",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/benhimself/{size}/2160_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-18T19:28:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A simple but kind of mindbending idea I had which I didn't go with:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>COHESIVE UNIT (Ongoing, limited)</em></p><p><em><span>H is reduced by 1.</span></em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It's a little game-breaking in certain situations, but so are quite a few other cards (next evolution versus certain opponents, say, or twist the ether versus single-source villains when teamed with Ra or AZ). It's a solid enough card that it's probably worth a drawback if I were to fully flesh out the idea, but I just dig how the mechanic fits into the theme: that of Legacy leading them as a well-knit team who can work more closely together than another team with similar numbers.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(Maybe something like: \"If a hero ongoing would be destroyed by anything other than itself, destroy Cohesive Unit instead\" or something, so it's more vulnerable to ongoing destruction? Or just \"At the start of Legacy's turn, you must either skip your play phase, skip your power phase, or destroy this card.\" to represent his effort coordinating the battle.)</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:04:03.319Z",
